Daniil TV: piece eviction for a bounded cache (libtorrent 2.1.2, 6da363d2994f17c0b3c0450d124cf73a31a73847)

Adds torrent_handle::evict_pieces(). Custom storage that keeps only a window
of a torrent discards verified pieces; libtorrent must then forget it has them,
or it would never download them again. On the network thread, each evicted
piece goes back to the piece picker as never downloaded (keeping its priority),
file progress is rebuilt, queued uploads are rejected, every peer supporting
lt_donthave (BEP 54) is told, seeds included (a seed that believes we have
everything drops us as redundant), other downloading BitTorrent peers are
disconnected once per call, and a finished or seeding torrent resumes if it
wants an evicted piece. A seed's dropped piece picker is rebuilt the way resume
data marks pieces, keeping pad-byte accounting intact. Merkle trees keep their
verified hashes. A former seed that downloads again makes the seeds and
upload-only peers it dropped as redundant reconnectable at once, instead of
after min_reconnect_time. The completion callback tells the storage it may free
the pieces once disk jobs issued before it complete.

TORRENT_HAS_EVICT_PIECES lets dependent code refuse to build without it.
Regressions: streaming/native/tests (eviction, re-download, seeds, v2, peers
without lt_donthave). Re-verify them before moving to another libtorrent.

